# Env OAuth token vs account binding

ccpool can read `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` from the process env or from
`~/.claude/settings.json` → `env` (see `packages/core/src/identity/credentials.ts`).
That unblocks the **usage poll** when there is no `.credentials.json` / keychain.

**Open issue the user may hit next:** group create/join still requires a hydrated
Claude `accountUuid` from `~/.claude.json` → `oauthAccount` (`resolveAccount`).
A friend who only injects the env token and never completed a normal Claude Code
login may fail `ccpool init` / account binding even though polling would work.

Symptom to watch for (from `probeSharedGroup` in `apps/cli/src/lib/setup.ts`):

> no onboarded Claude account on this machine — sign into Claude Code first

If the user reports that, fix or work around the missing `oauthAccount`
hydration path — do not assume the env-token credential change alone is enough.
